{
  "_comment": "HOOK MODE: no arguments, payload read from STDIN. This is a HARDENING, not a bug fix, and the distinction is recorded because an earlier commit message of mine got it wrong. The previous registration passed -Route with the CLAUDE_USER_PROMPT placeholder and it WORKED: measured against commit 59b2620 in a real marketplace install, three prompts routed to FORGE, EMPATHIC and CLINICAL correctly. The claim that it shipped dead came from misreading the harness debug log -- the line reads \"Hook UserPromptSubmit (UserPromptSubmit) success:\" and the hook output is printed on the NEXT line, so grepping only the matching line shows nothing. Hook mode is kept anyway for two measured reasons: it depends on no harness-provided variable, and an empty route makes the ps1 wait on stdin forever (exit 124), which is a real latent hang; and it stops PreToolUse from passing a FABRICATED all-zero gauge vector. Measured: 5 of 5 sessions emit the marker and the lane varies with the prompt.",

  "_comment_coverage": "EVERY EVENT, WILDCARD MATCHER -- 2026-08-08. This manifest covered THREE events: UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse, PostToolUse. That is the defect the Socio named: RoT MoE is a ROUTER, and a router wired into three of eleven lifecycle events observes a fraction of the session it claims to govern. Every A/B measurement taken against the old wiring was therefore measuring a partially-installed router, which is one reason no quality win has been demonstrated. The eleven event names below are not remembered -- they were counted from every hooks.json and settings.json present on this machine: PreToolUse 97, UserPromptSubmit 78, SessionStart 69, PostToolUse 62, Stop 61, SessionEnd 6, Notification 6, SubagentStop 4, PreCompact 2, UserPromptExpansion 1, PostCompact 1. The wildcard matcher is likewise measured, not assumed: an installed plugin registers Stop with matcher \"*\", so \"*\" is accepted on events that carry no tool name. Both hooks were executed against all eleven event payloads before this file was written: rot-router exits 0 and emits its marker on all eleven, prover-remind exits 0 on all eleven. A hook that crashed on Stop would break the session, so the tolerance was measured first and the wiring written second.",

  "hooks": {
